            "review_text": "jenn89154943\nVancouver, Canada84 contributions\n0\nExpensive and pushy\nMar 2016 • Couples\nOur hotel told our cab driver to take us to a specific restaurant. Cab dropped us off here and it wasn't where the hotel advised him to take us to. We went inside the restaurant anyway and it's a huge location. So big that it took 2 ppl to seat us at a table. Once we sat down the menus were given to us and the server just stood there the whole time over our shoulders while we were looking which is very uncomfortable especially when you don't know the menu. He then brought another menu and forced us to look at it saying \"better items! Better items!\" When i looked it was filled with options of rabbit, snake, turtles. All prices around 2 million dong or more. Which is completely ridiculous but he kept trying to push us on that menu. When I picked some items that I wanted, the menu said 65,000 dong for some snails. He then proceeded to flip to another menu and said I can only buy it by the kilo which was 1.5 million dong?! That made no sense as some items did say X price per kilo but these didn't. We ended up just getting up and leaving. This place is a huge rip off to foreigners, I don't know how they have such a large location. I really doubt he makes locals order things by the kilo. I don't know about the taste but with the menu and the behavior of the staff I won't be going back\nRead more\nWritten March 10, 2016",
